    why: "Substance use is common in adult ADHD and can mimic, mask or worsen it. The key tests are the order of onset and how the person is during substance-free periods. In population surveys ADHD began before the substance use disorder in most people with both. Use also matters for treatment: assess the risk of misuse and diversion before any stimulant. Do not rate symptoms while the person is intoxicated or in withdrawal.",
    src: "WHO ICD-11 CDDR; Fayyad et al. 2017; NICE NG87 1.7.4",
